{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli a noble family that ruled the County of Tripoli. He was the son of Bohemond III of Tripoli and his wife Orguine de Harenc. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1184. He died in 1187 and was succeeded by his son Bohemond IV.\n\n* **Life and Death** *\nRaymond III was a prominent figure in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He married a woman named Eschiva of Arsur but the marriage was childless. He later married a woman named Alice of Armenia but this marriage also produced no children. Raymond III died in 1187 during the reign of King Guy of Jerusalem.\n\n* **Military Campaigns** *\nRaymond III took part in the Third Crusade led by King Richard I of England. He also fought in the Battle of Cresson in 1192 where the Crusaders defeated the forces of Saladin. Raymond III died before the Battle of Hattin in 1187 which was a significant defeat for the Crusaders.\n\nThe County of Tripoli was a Crusader state established in 1104. It was located in the Levant region of the Middle East. The County of Tripoli was a vassal of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. The County of Tripoli was a significant power in the region and played a key role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\n* **Family and Succession** *\nRaymond III married twice and had no children from either marriage. He was succeeded by his son Bohemond IV who went on to become a prominent figure in the politics of the County of Tripoli. Bohemond IV was married to a woman named Plaisance of Antioch and had several children with her.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.021772763}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00021634146}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0012805604}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.12215032}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.8980677e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00026020003},